 A `null` value in the patch removes the corresponding member from the target. Any non-object patch
 (including arrays) replaces the target wholesale.
+
+### `createPatch(from, to)`
+
+Computes a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) that turns `from` into `to` when
+applied with `applyPatch`. Neither input is modified. The patch only contains operations for the
+parts of the document that actually changed.
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+createPatch({ foo: "bar" }, { foo: "baz" });
+// [{ op: "replace", path: "/foo", value: "baz" }]
+```
+
+Array elements are compared by index: elements common to both arrays are diffed recursively, and
+any extra elements are added or removed at the end.
